KG42.register("clusters-fc1487c2c04b8d7b3baec1ff",{"id":"31-coalition_formation::v142-d-CL002","paper":"31-coalition_formation","label":"Price-threshold-driven hourly coalition selection and quantity adjustment","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL002","label":"Price-threshold-driven hourly coalition selection and quantity adjustment","market_meaning":"After household demand is processed, with residual energy deficit, available P2P prices and individual thresholds as conditions, prosumers select the trading state and provider/receiver role; then, according to supply-demand branches, quantities are corrected, members are determined, and hourly merging and splitting are performed. The result is candidate coalition members and adjustment quantities; the existing conditions and mathematical steps are not yet sufficient to guarantee that all branches achieve total-quantity balance.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","coordination","matching","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"The chains together cover the initial prices, state selection, quantity adjustment and member reorganization of Algorithm 1. The conditions in Table 2 and equations (20)-(22), the indexing of over-demand members, and the timing of price adoption remain inconsistent or unclear, and cannot be regarded as a closed algorithm.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Quantity correction directly affects membership, and the price-threshold decision selects the provider/receiver to be adjusted, so the three main chains constitute the same coalition formation activity. The shared pricing chain provides only the initial signal interface; final transaction pricing and execution remain in another cluster.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide quantity correction under supply-demand imbalance and the total-quantity balance objective, which directly affect final member selection."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide individual thresholds and the charging/discharging/state decision conditions of Table 2."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Translate states, utility comparison and adjusted quantities into provider/receiver sets and coalition reorganization."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Only share C003's initial quotes and corresponding price objects as decision inputs; do not automatically replace the state 2 final price with the same signal."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CN01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-pc","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-pd","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-th-pc","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-th-pd","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E23"],"rationale":"Algorithm 1 first sets initial charging/discharging prices, and then lets applicable prosumers use Table 2; these prices are outputs in the pricing chain and comparison inputs in the coordination chain, and their local roles are retained."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CN02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C013","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C014","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C016"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g02-E38"],"rationale":"The source connects the state selection formed by threshold comparison to coalition and provider/receiver selection; the algorithm's positive energy-deficit branching precedes the application of Table 2, and the condition conflict in equations (20)-(22) is retained as a gap, without claiming that the representations are equivalent."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL002-CN03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-e-nd","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-e-mc","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::x_e_nd","v141-c-R004::x::x_e_mc","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C017"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21"],"rationale":"The two chains cover quantity reduction and subsequent member determination in the same Algorithm 1 branch. The over-demand branch confirms only the interface between the adjustment quantity and the member test; it does not eliminate the ambiguity between the test-quantity index m and the decision-maker index n."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R004::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21"],"rationale":"Both places reference the same frozen clearing node and jointly bear the quantity adjustment of Algorithm 1; the representative selection is only for display and does not merge all constraints of the two chains."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R007::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R007::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E23"],"rationale":"The three places are references to the same frozen pricing node; identical nodes do not mean that the initial price, individual threshold and state 2 final price are the same quantity."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM03","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-pc","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-th-pc","v141-c-R004::theta::theta_pc"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E23"],"rationale":"The same algorithm's initial P2P charging price serves as output or input in setting, state comparison and member selection respectively; retain the x/theta classification, unit formulations and local roles, and it does not concern the final price with the s2 subscript."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-pd","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-th-pd","v141-c-R004::theta::theta_pd"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E23"],"rationale":"The same algorithm's initial P2P discharging price is passed across the setting and decision steps; retain each object's output/input role, and do not merge it with the state 2 final price."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-th-pnc","v141-c-R004::theta::theta_pnc"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E06","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E38"],"rationale":"The algorithm explicitly invokes the individual charging threshold defined in equation (11) for state and member determination; preserve the different local uses of threshold calculation and matching comparison."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-th-pnd","v141-c-R004::theta::theta_pnd"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E09","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E38"],"rationale":"The algorithm explicitly invokes the individual discharging threshold defined in equation (13); identical thresholds do not automatically make different member conditions equivalent."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM07","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-e-nd","v141-c-R004::x::x_e_nd"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21"],"rationale":"The two places are references to the same provider battery discharge quantity in correction and member determination; retain the before- and after-update semantics and the original unit declarations; do not treat the values before and after update as equal, and do not deduplicate R004-C001 as a whole, since it contains member conditions."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM08","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-e-mc","v141-c-R004::x::x_e_mc"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21"],"rationale":"The two places correspond to the receiver charging quantity in Algorithm 1; retain the adjustment and matching roles and the update stage; this mapping does not resolve the n/m ambiguity of the subsequent member decision-maker."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM09","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-K","v141-c-R004::theta::theta_K"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21"],"rationale":"The provider count in the same algorithm branch is used for summation and as the reduction divisor; retain the two indices and local roles, do not equate the count object with a set, and do not presume it equals the count in the final pricing stage."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM10","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta-L","v141-c-R004::theta::theta_L"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21"],"rationale":"The receiver count in the same algorithm branch is used for summation and as the reduction divisor; preserve the distinction between the count, the set, and the count in the final pricing stage."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL002-OM11","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C017"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E21"],"rationale":"The two express the same quantity adjustment in lines 35-38 of Algorithm 1 under the same over-demand condition; one updates in place, and the other uses a prime symbol to denote the result. Retain the representation and the core/support roles, do not count it again as a new adjustment rule, and do not include the ambiguous member test."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G01","category":"unverified_source","description":"The connections and object correspondences in this cluster are based only on unreviewed candidate evidence permitted by the experiment; B's unverified status remains unchanged.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E38"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the actual printed content of the algorithm, tables and formulas, and independently inspect the condition combinations of this cluster."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"When some individual quantities are less than the average reduction amount, the total reduction from taking the smaller value one by one in a single pass may be less than the supply-demand excess. The frozen step does not provide residual reallocation or iteration, and therefore it cannot be guaranteed that after R001-C002/C003 are completed the balance objective of R001-C001 is achieved.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C017"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E31"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check whether the source has additional reallocation, repeated execution or applicable conditions; before upstream supplementation, retain the unclosed relationship between quantity adjustment and the balance obligation."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G03","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The comparison direction of the receiver discharge price in equation (20) is inconsistent with Table 2 case 1; equations (20)-(21) also do not clearly accommodate the situation in case 4 where a provider is selected through utility comparison. R004-C016 cannot be treated as an equivalent member definition to R002-C003 or R004-C014.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C014","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C016"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E021","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E38","v141-b-g03-E09"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check item by item the comparison signs and branch applicability scope of Table 2 and equations (20)-(22), and have upstream clarify the member-selection criterion; no unified rewriting may be made in D."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G04","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The over-demand branch tests the adjusted e_{m,c}(t), but the member decision-maker is printed as Prosumer n. The quantity adjustment can correspond, but the specific member mapping from receiver to V/W remains unclear.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C017"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E21"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the participant indices in lines 39-42 of Algorithm 1, and after confirmation have upstream complete the member expression; for now, do not automatically change n to m."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G05","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The frozen Pareto definition retains the printed condition that at least one person's utility is equal, which cannot automatically be interpreted as the usual strict improvement condition. The mathematical closure between this preference and merge/split termination and stability has not been established by the existing chains.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C006","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C015"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E024","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E15","v141-b-g02-E16"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the equality condition in Definition 1 and how it is adopted in merging and splitting, and independently inspect the termination and improvement arguments; keep the frozen comparison expression unchanged."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G06","category":"upstream_missing","description":"Table 2 case 4 and R004-C014 invoke charging/discharging utility and its maximum value, but the frozen chains do not fully include equations (5)-(6), the optimal quantity response and the corresponding objects of the feasible region. Role selection when utilities are equal is also not given.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C014","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-e-nd","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x-e-mc"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E012","v141-b-g02-E06","v141-b-g02-E08","v141-b-g02-E38","v141-b-g03-E10"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream is to supplement source-supported representations of utility, optimal response and feasible range, and check the boundaries of each extracted version of equation (22); where no source exists for a tie-breaking rule, leave it blank."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G07","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The initial mid-market-derived signal and the state 2 final price in equations (18)-(19) use different symbols and stages. The existing chains do not clarify whether the final price feeds back into Table 2 or again changes members and quantities.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-pd-s2","v141-c-R007::x::v141-c-R007-x-pc-s2"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-M01-E24","v141-b-g02-E32","v141-b-g02-E33"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Clarify the adoption timing and applicable objects of the initial decision and the final transaction price; when there is no source explanation, keep the price objects separate and do not add feedback or iteration."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G08","category":"ontology_extension","description":"This cluster assembles member selection and reorganization; it cannot thereby treat stability, uniqueness, maximum social welfare or prosumer-centric properties as proven results. The complete verification content has not entered these frozen chains, and the related proposal remains unapproved.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C008","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C009","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C015"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g03-E08","v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g03-E12","v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g03-E19"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g03-P02","v141-b-g03-P03"],"required_work":"Manually review the framework attribution of the verification concepts; if these properties need to be covered, upstream should independently organize the definitions and arguments and check their premises; the boundary decisions of this cluster cannot replace scientific verification."}]},"rule_refs":["31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R001","31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R002","31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R004","31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R007"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-2b41ecf17cc33e3a","COMP-2d6ad9d125effd47","COMP-bfd4e5f3b6ab7697","COMP-c2c63e68e8427440","COMP-e02ca159eb62d0e4"]});
